WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
Speaker 1: Welcome back to the David Packman&nbsp;
Show. I'm producer Pat Forde, filling in for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.640
David today while he's away. Some pretty big&nbsp;
news broke yesterday, which is that Hunter Biden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.680
the son of President Joe Biden, has reached a&nbsp;
tentative agreement with federal prosecutors to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:20.160
plead guilty to two minor tax charges and to&nbsp;
admit to the facts of a gun charge. The plea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:25.200
deal will likely keep Hunter Biden out of jail&nbsp;
and it subject to approval by a federal judge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.660
which is likely going to happen. The proposed&nbsp;
deal includes pleading guilty to two misdemeanor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:37.380
tax charges for failure to pay taxes in 2017 and&nbsp;
2018, with a combined liability of approximately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:44.100
$1.2 million. Prosecutors are going to recommend&nbsp;
probation for the tax charges, and then the gun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:49.800
charge is going to be handled as a diversion case&nbsp;
where Hunter will be able to technically not have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:55.560
to plead guilty to the crime and he'll be able&nbsp;
to do so if he successfully meets the measures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:01.740
outlined in the diversion program. The gun charge&nbsp;
will ultimately likely be removed from his record.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:07.860
So Hunter Biden's gun charge stems from a false&nbsp;
statement that he made on paperwork while he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:15.180
purchasing a gun. He denied drug use or having a&nbsp;
drug problem when in fact that wasn't true. Lying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:20.640
on gun purchase forms is only a small percentage&nbsp;
of firearm related prosecutions, and typically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:26.280
it's tacked on as a secondary offense. And that&nbsp;
seems to be what happened here. Hunter Biden's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.840
lawyer stated that he takes responsibility for&nbsp;
the tax mistakes made during a period of turmoil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:36.120
and addiction in his life. The full statement from&nbsp;
his lawyer, Chris Clark, was, quote, Hunter will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:42.300
take responsibility for two instances of failure&nbsp;
to file tax payments. When do a firearm charge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:48.060
which will be subject to a pretrial diversion&nbsp;
agreement and will not be the subject of the plea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.980
agreement will also be filed by the government.&nbsp;
I know Hunter believes it is important to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:58.500
responsibility for these mistakes he made during&nbsp;
a period of turmoil and addiction in his life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.960
He looks forward to continuing his recovery and&nbsp;
moving forward. The White House, for its part,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:08.340
has expressed support for Hunter Biden, stating&nbsp;
that the president and the first lady love their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:14.700
son and support his efforts to rebuild his life.&nbsp;
So I hear all this information and I think that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.980
All right, it looks like justice has been served.&nbsp;
Hunter Biden clearly did some stuff wrong and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.880
appears to have committed some crimes here. He&nbsp;
didn't pay taxes that he owed to the federal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.560
government. That effectively is stealing from&nbsp;
the rest of us. And so he should have to pay his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:34.740
fair share just like anybody else. He did lie&nbsp;
while going through the process of obtaining a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:39.540
weapon. And you can't say that you're not using&nbsp;
drugs when going through that process when you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:44.280
actually are at the time. You may disagree&nbsp;
about whether that should be illegal or not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:50.220
but the law says that it is currently and so,&nbsp;
sure, he should be held accountable for it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.120
And I think that the correct agreement was&nbsp;
ultimately reached here. He takes the plea deal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.620
he gets a slap on the wrist with the probation.&nbsp;
He doesn't have to go to jail or anything like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.360
that. It doesn't seem to me like these amount to&nbsp;
jail worthy crimes. Anyway, we can end it now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.160
Right? This is really not all that hard.&nbsp;
And I don't look at this case and think,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.200
Oh, I have to defend Hunter Biden at all costs.&nbsp;
I really don't care about Hunter Biden. Right. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:18.180
apply the same standard when it comes to anyone&nbsp;
facing criminal charges. Right. Whether it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.640
Trump, whether it's Biden, Hillary, whoever.&nbsp;
If there's something to investigate, you should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.320
investigate. If there's something to charge, then&nbsp;
you should charge. If it can be proven in court,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.240
then go ahead and prove it. And ultimately, if&nbsp;
a sentence is warranted, whether that be sending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:38.220
someone to prison or otherwise, then sentence&nbsp;
them appropriately. But with the MAGA folks, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:44.820
pretend as though Hunter Biden this whole time&nbsp;
has been like Al Capone or Charles Manson, when in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:50.100
reality these are pretty minor charges and at the&nbsp;
same time they defend Donald Trump no matter what.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:56.220
When he's accused of keeping the nation's&nbsp;
top secrets in his bathroom at Mar a Lago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:00.480
that anyone can just stumble upon if they knew&nbsp;
their way around the resort. And he, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:06.240
refused to give the documents back after months&nbsp;
and months of the National Archives asking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.680
And that's just one of the multiple criminal&nbsp;
investigations and now criminal prosecutions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:16.680
that Donald Trump is dealing with. Also relevant&nbsp;
to this is the fact that Donald Trump was actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:21.360
president and wants to be president again.&nbsp;
Whereas Hunter Biden, I hate to break it to you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:25.680
but he's actually not the president. He just so&nbsp;
happens to be related to the current president. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.720
is the son of the president. But that doesn't mean&nbsp;
that he is the president. He doesn't even work in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:35.520
his father's administration. We've, of course,&nbsp;
discussed this ad nauseum. But I suppose the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:41.400
question now is, how is the Republican Party going&nbsp;
to react to the news of Hunter Biden taking this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:46.620
plea deal? Because they can do a couple of things&nbsp;
